  "description": "Decision 245 section 2's recording (phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7): a virtual Normal on a UV-islanded set whose Height has no layer, with a bound Normal mesh map, under Legacy at 256 px, OpenGL. API probe golden on the authored sphere (one set uzp_sphere, pole rows half covered): the initial Paint root is deleted by the guarded one-shot cleanup (step 2, owned create, exactly one PaintLayer, no root left); the authored 16-bit normal-b is bound as the Normal mesh map; one visible Split fill with only Normal active carries the authored 16-bit normal-a, Normal at opacity 1, neutral geometry mask, identity Nearest Repeat UV. Fresh getters read the full root tree, the fill state, both resource joins, the fill source and the mesh map in same_session and after Full save/reopen, with no setter replayed. Captures in both recordings: Normal_OpenGL at PNG 16 and OpenEXR 32f with infinite and passthrough padding, and an OpenEXR 32f infinite control of Height, the Normal channel and normal_base, each export done twice in a row, keyed by step, no dithering. Expected bits, void rules and predictions are declared in parity/reports/phase1/normal-empty-height-freeze.md before capture; the Height control is an observation, not proof of the virtual normal's internal Height.",
